                            <comment id="432458" author="yujian" created="Thu, 24 Oct 2024 06:17:29 +0000">&lt;p&gt;The failure occurred 5 times in the past 6 months.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="432604" author="lixi_wc" created="Fri, 25 Oct 2024 02:53:52 +0000">&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ys" class="user-hover" rel="ys"&gt;ys&lt;/a&gt; Would you please check this issue? &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="439748" author="emoly.liu" created="Wed, 25 Dec 2024 02:59:04 +0000">&lt;p&gt;+1 on master: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/8736bdd3-2bf6-43e9-9aab-39805164f69b" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/8736bdd3-2bf6-43e9-9aab-39805164f69b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;BTW, 13 timeout records in the past 4 weeks.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="446832" author="ys" created="Thu, 6 Mar 2025 03:08:45 +0000">&lt;p&gt;I have looked through the many kind of "wait delete timed out" error cases. Seems they all have logs:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;
Delete is not completed in 28 seconds
CMD: trevis-101vm6 /usr/sbin/lctl get_param osc.*MDT*.sync_*
osc.lustre-OST0000-osc-MDT0000.sync_changes=0
osc.lustre-OST0000-osc-MDT0000.sync_in_flight=0
osc.lustre-OST0000-osc-MDT0000.sync_in_progress=1
osc.lustre-OST0000-osc-MDT0002.sync_changes=0
osc.lustre-OST0000-osc-MDT0002.sync_in_flight=0

&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This indicted a osp request stuck in commit phase. I think we should add a some debug code in test script to figure out why it was delayed. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="507124" author="JIRAUSER24100" created="Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:04:20 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Closing as fixed by the later wait_delete_completed rework. Rainshadow shows six failures of this signature (the last "wait delete timed out" on 2024-11-25, a timeout in the same test on 2024-12-23) and none in the 400 days since (checked 2025-10-23 to 2026-11-26), with replay-single test_89 still running in CI. In that time &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20076" title="reduce testing time by optimizing test and test-framework.sh" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20076"&gt;LU-20076&lt;/a&gt; rewrote the delete wait (commits dc6eecf0d0 "fewer remote commands to wait for deletes", 7bfcbd74e1 "commit OST destroys when waiting for them", 0569c2b815, and 0990db68d7 "let replay-single 89 wait for statfs caches") on current master. The old waiter only polled osp sync_in_progress and did not force the OST to commit its destroys, which matches the stuck-in-commit symptom described in the comments. Not reproduced on a VM; this rests on CI history. Please reopen with a Maloo link if it recurs.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
